was 2.67)\n\n**CI:** run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNote: this changes how every exact half-cent value is rounded. Half the ties now round down instead of up. Callers that depend on the old half-up behavior should be checked.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 387068, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Dexmpj6rqjSsyJrYDwLo3q", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-fin-212-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 387068, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Dexmpj6rqjSsyJrYDwLo3q", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 392289, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). So `2.665` came out as `2.67`, but the test expects `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was a one-line change, plus the import.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**Things to know:**\n- I didn't merge it, since merging into main needs a code owner's approval.\n- I couldn't find FIN-212 in the security advisory lookup. It's probably an internal ticket. The test and the docstring already said what was needed, so I didn't need it.\n- The PR description notes that this changes how all exact half-cent amounts are rounded: half of them now round down instead of up. Any code that depends on the old behavior should be checked.", "error": null}]